.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_GET_CURRENT_CIPHER 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_get_current_cipher ,
.Nm SSL_get_cipher_name ,
.Nm SSL_get_cipher ,
.Nm SSL_get_cipher_bits ,
.Nm SSL_get_cipher_version ,
.Nm SSL_get_pending_cipher
.Nd get SSL_CIPHER of a connection
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft const SSL_CIPHER *
.Fo SSL_get_current_cipher
.Fa "const SSL *ssl"
.Fc
.Ft const SSL_CIPHER *
.Fo SSL_get_pending_cipher
.Fa "const SSL *ssl"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fo SSL_get_cipher_name
.Fa "const SSL *s"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fo SSL_get_cipher
.Fa "const SSL *s"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_get_cipher_bits
.Fa "const SSL *s"
.Fa "int *np"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fo SSL_get_cipher_version
.Fa "const SSL *s"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_get_current_cipher
returns a pointer to an SSL_CIPHER object containing the description of
the actually used cipher of a connection established with the
.Fa ssl
object.
.Fa ssl
.Sy MUST NOT
be NULL. See
.Xr SSL_CIPHER_get_name 3
for more details.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_get_cipher_name
obtains the name of the currently used cipher.
.Fn SSL_get_cipher
is identical to
.Fn SSL_get_cipher_name .
.Fn SSL_get_cipher_bits
is a macro to obtain the number of secret/algorithm bits used and
.Fn SSL_get_cipher_version
returns the protocol name.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_get_pending_cipher
returns a pointer to an SSL_CIPHER object containing the description of
the cipher (if any) that has been negotiated for future use on the
connection established with the
.Fa ssl
object, but is not yet in use.
This may be the case during handshake processing, when control flow can
be returned to the application via any of several callback methods.
The internal sequencing of handshake processing and callback invocation
is not guaranteed to be stable from release to release, and at present
only the callback set by
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_alpn_select_cb 3
is guaranteed to have a non-NULL return value.
Other callbacks may be added to this list over time.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SSL_get_current_cipher
returns the cipher actually used, or NULL if no session has been
established.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_get_pending_cipher
returns the cipher to be used at the next change of cipher suite, or
NULL if no such cipher is known.
.Sh NOTES
SSL_get_cipher, SSL_get_cipher_bits, SSL_get_cipher_version, and
SSL_get_cipher_name are implemented as macros.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssl 7 ,
.Xr SSL_CIPHER_get_name 3
